    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-22a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22A Special residence requirement—persons engaging in activities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-22a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "that are of benefit to Australia\n\n(1) Subject to this section, for the purposes of section 21 a person (the\napplicant) satisfies the special residence requirement if:\n\n(a) the following apply:\n\nAmendments relating to special residence requirement  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Citizenship Test Review and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 90, 2009            7\n\n(i) the applicant is seeking to engage in an activity\nspecified under subsection 22C(1);\n\n(ii) the applicant’s engagement in that activity would be of\nbenefit to Australia;\n\n(iii) the applicant needs to be an Australian citizen in order\nto engage in that activity;\n\n(iv) in order for the applicant to engage in that activity, there\nis insufficient time for the applicant to satisfy the\ngeneral residence requirement (see section 22); and\n\n(b) the head of an organisation specified under subsection\n22C(2), or a person whom the Minister is satisfied holds a\nsenior position in that organisation, has given the Minister a\nnotice in writing stating that the applicant has a reasonable\nprospect of being engaged in that activity; and\n\n(c) the applicant was present in Australia for a total of at least\n180 days during the period of 2 years immediately before the\nday the applicant made the application; and\n\n(d) the applicant was present in Australia for a total of at least 90\ndays during the period of 12 months immediately before the\nday the applicant made the application; and\n\n(e) the applicant was ordinarily resident in Australia throughout\nthe period of 2 years immediately before the day the\napplicant made the application; and\n\n(f) the applicant was a permanent resident for the period of 2\nyears immediately before the day the applicant made the\napplication; and\n\n(g) the applicant was not present in Australia as an unlawful\nnon-citizen at any time during the period of 2 years\nimmediately before the day the applicant made the\napplication.\nConfinement in prison or psychiatric institution\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the applicant is taken not to satisfy\nparagraph (1)(c) if, at any time during the 2 year period mentioned\nin that paragraph, the applicant was:\n\n(a) confined in a prison; or\n\n(b) confined in a psychiatric institution by order of a court made\nin connection with proceedings for an offence against an\nAustralian law in relation to the applicant.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendments relating to special residence requirement",
      "skos:definition": "that are of benefit to Australia\n\n(1) Subject to this section, for the purposes of section 21 a person (the\napplicant) satisfies the special residence requirement if:\n\n(a) the following apply:\n\nAmendments relating to special residence requirement  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Citizenship Test Review and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 90, 2009            7\n\n(i) the applicant is seeking to engage in an activity\nspecified under subsection 22C(1);\n\n(ii) the applicant’s engagement in that activity would be of\nbenefit to Australia;\n\n(iii) the applicant needs to be an Australian citizen in order\nto engage in that activity;\n\n(iv) in order for the applicant to engage in that activity, there\nis insufficient time for the applicant to satisfy the\ngeneral residence requirement (see section 22); and\n\n(b) the head of an organisation specified under subsection\n22C(2), or a person whom the Minister is satisfied holds a\nsenior position in that organisation, has given the Minister a\nnotice in writing stating that the applicant has a reasonable\nprospect of being engaged in that activity; and\n\n(c) the applicant was present in Australia for a total of at least\n180 days during the period of 2 years immediately before the\nday the applicant made the application; and\n\n(d) the applicant was present in Australia for a total of at least 90\ndays during the period of 12 months immediately before the\nday the applicant made the application; and\n\n(e) the applicant was ordinarily resident in Australia throughout\nthe period of 2 years immediately before the day the\napplicant made the application; and\n\n(f) the applicant was a permanent resident for the period of 2\nyears immediately before the day the applicant made the\napplication; and\n\n(g) the applicant was not present in Australia as an unlawful\nnon-citizen at any time during the period of 2 years\nimmediately before the day the applicant made the\napplication.\nConfinement in prison or psychiatric institution\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-22a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-22a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8f25da2b3ee8388e5c8631d3267155f23cae5caef7d279213c7c15033afa4a88"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-test-review-and-other-measures-act-2009#sch-2-sec-22a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22A Special residence requirement—persons engaging in activities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "that are of benefit to Australia\n\n(1) Subject to this section, for the purposes of section 21 a person (the\napplicant) satisfies the special residence requirement if:\n\n(a) the following apply:\n\nAmendments relating to special residence requirement  Schedule 2\n\nAustralian Citizenship Amendment (Citizenship Test Review and Other Measures) Act 2009\nNo. 90, 2009            7\n\n(i) the applicant is seeking to engage in an activity\nspecified under subsection 22C(1);\n\n(ii) the applicant’s engagement in that activity would be of\nbenefit to Australia;\n\n(iii) the applicant needs to be an Australian citizen in order\nto engage in that activity;\n\n(iv) in order for the applicant to engage in that activity, there\nis insufficient time for the applicant to satisfy the\ngeneral residence requirement (see section 22); and\n\n(b) the head of an organisation specified under subsection\n22C(2), or a person whom the Minister is satisfied holds a\nsenior position in that organisation, has given the Minister a\nnotice in writing stating that the applicant has a reasonable\nprospect of being engaged in that activity; and\n\n(c) the applicant was present in Australia for a total of at least\n180 days during the period of 2 years immediately before the\nday the applicant made the application; and\n\n(d) the applicant was present in Australia for a total of at least 90\ndays during the period of 12 months immediately before the\nday the applicant made the application; and\n\n(e) the applicant was ordinarily resident in Australia throughout\nthe period of 2 years immediately before the day the\napplicant made the application; and\n\n(f) the applicant was a permanent resident for the period of 2\nyears immediately before the day the applicant made the\napplication; and\n\n(g) the applicant was not present in Australia as an unlawful\nnon-citizen at any time during the period of 2 years\nimmediately before the day the applicant made the\napplication.\nConfinement in prison or psychiatric institution\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the applicant is taken not to satisfy\nparagraph (1)(c) if, at any time during the 2 year period mentioned\nin that paragraph, the applicant was:\n\n(a) confined in a prison; or\n\n(b) confined in a psychiatric institution by order of a court made\nin connection with proceedings for an offence against an\nAustralian law in relation to the applicant.\n\nSchedule 2  Amendments relating to special residence requirement"
    },
